IMPORT `snap-core`

-- Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 (7 U.S.C. ch. 51), section 2020, subsections (f) to (n).
-- LAYER 1 (the law, objectively). Same reading of results as snap4-s2020-a-d.l4: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING.
-- The text is the converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text.

-- repealed: 1562 | (f) is shown repealed: "(f) Repealed. Pub. L. 111-296, title II, § 241(b)(2), Dec. 13, 2010, 124 Stat. 3236"

§ `s 2020(g) State noncompliance; correction of failures`

-- src:1564 | If the Secretary determines, upon information received by the Secretary, investigation initiated by the Secretary, or investigation that the Secretary shall initiate upon receiving sufficient information evidencing a pattern of lack of compliance by a State agency of a type specified in this subsection, that in the administration of the supplemental nutrition assistance program there is a failure by a State agency without good cause to comply with any of the provisions of this chapter, the regulations issued pursuant to this chapter, the State plan of operation submitted pursuant to subsection (d) of this section, the State plan for automated data processing submitted pursuant to subsection (o)(2) of this section, or the requirements established pursuant to section 2032 of this title the Secretary shall immediately inform such State agency of such failure and shall allow the State agency a specified period of time for the correction of such failure. …
-- jural: the State agency | the Secretary | claim and duty: the Secretary immediately informs the State agency of the failure and allows a specified period to correct it
@ref s 2020(g) (src:1564)
GIVEN `the Secretary determines that in the administration of the supplemental nutrition assistance program there is a failure by a State agency without good cause to comply with the chapter, its regulations, the State plan of operation, the State plan for automated data processing, or the requirements under section 2032` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(g) the Secretary must immediately inform the State agency of the failure and allow a specified period for its correction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Secretary determines that in the administration of the supplemental nutrition assistance program there is a failure by a State agency without good cause to comply with the chapter, its regulations, the State plan of operation, the State plan for automated data processing, or the requirements under section 2032`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Secretary's determination was not supplied
    WHEN JUST determined THEN
        IF determined THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Secretary determines ... that in the administration of the supplemental nutrition assistance program there is a failure by a State agency without good cause to comply"

-- src:1564 | If the State agency does not correct such failure within that specified period, the Secretary may refer the matter to the Attorney General with a request that injunctive relief be sought to require compliance forthwith by the State agency and, upon suit by the Attorney General in an appropriate district court of the United States …
-- jural: the Secretary | the State agency | power and liability: referral to the Attorney General for injunctive relief
@ref s 2020(g) (src:1564)
GIVEN `the Secretary has made the determination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency corrects the failure within the specified period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(g) the Secretary may refer the matter to the Attorney General with a request that injunctive relief be sought` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Secretary has made the determination` AND (NOT `the State agency corrects the failure within the specified period`) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF NOT `the Secretary has made the determination`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Secretary determines ... that in the administration of the supplemental nutrition assistance program there is a failure by a State agency without good cause to comply"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the State agency does not correct such failure within that specified period, the Secretary may refer the matter to the Attorney General"

-- src:1564 | and, upon suit by the Attorney General in an appropriate district court of the United States having jurisdiction of the geographic area in which the State agency is located and a showing that noncompliance has occurred, appropriate injunctive relief shall issue, …
-- jural: the Secretary | the State agency | power and liability: injunctive relief on a showing of noncompliance
@ref s 2020(g) (src:1564)
GIVEN `the Attorney General sues in an appropriate district court of the United States having jurisdiction of the geographic area in which the State agency is located` IS A BOOLEAN
      `noncompliance has been shown to have occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(g) appropriate injunctive relief shall issue` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Attorney General sues in an appropriate district court of the United States having jurisdiction of the geographic area in which the State agency is located` AND `noncompliance has been shown to have occurred` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "upon suit by the Attorney General in an appropriate district court ... and a showing that noncompliance has occurred"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1564 | the Secretary shall proceed to withhold from the State such funds authorized under sections 2025(a), 2025(c), and 2025(g) of this title as the Secretary determines to be appropriate, subject to administrative and judicial review under section 2023 of this title.
-- jural: the State | the Secretary | power and liability: funds under sections 2025(a), (c) and (g) withheld as appropriate, subject to review under section 2023
@ref s 2020(g) (src:1564)
GIVEN `the Secretary has made the determination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency corrects the failure within the specified period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(g) the Secretary must proceed to withhold the funds the Secretary determines to be appropriate` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Secretary has made the determination` AND (NOT `the State agency corrects the failure within the specified period`) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF NOT `the Secretary has made the determination`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Secretary determines ... that in the administration of the supplemental nutrition assistance program there is a failure by a State agency without good cause to comply"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the State agency does not correct such failure within that specified period, ... the Secretary shall proceed to withhold from the State such funds"

§ `s 2020(h) Deposit by State to cover fraudulently or negligently issued benefits`

-- src:1566 | If the Secretary determines that there has been negligence or fraud on the part of the State agency in the certification of applicant households, the State shall, upon request of the Secretary, deposit into the Treasury of the United States, a sum equal to the face value of any benefits issued as a result of such negligence or fraud.
-- jural: the Treasury of the United States | the State | claim and duty: a deposit of the face value of benefits issued through the State agency's negligence or fraud
@ref s 2020(h) (src:1566)
GIVEN `the Secretary determines that there has been negligence or fraud on the part of the State agency in the certification of applicant households` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary has requested the deposit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the face value of the benefits issued as a result of the negligence or fraud, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2020(h) the sum the State must deposit into the Treasury of the United States` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Secretary determines that there has been negligence or fraud on the part of the State agency in the certification of applicant households`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Secretary's determination was not supplied
    WHEN JUST determined THEN
        BRANCH
            IF determined AND `the Secretary has requested the deposit` THEN JUST `the face value of the benefits issued as a result of the negligence or fraud, in dollars`
            IF NOT determined THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states a sum only where the Secretary has determined negligence or fraud, and a sum has no value that says no sum is due; the result type cannot carry the text's no
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "upon request of the Secretary"
            OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 2020(i) Application and denial procedures`

-- src:1569 | Notwithstanding any other provision of law, households in which all members are applicants for or recipients of supplemental security income shall be informed of the availability of benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program and be assisted in making a simple application to participate in such program at the social security office and be certified for eligibility utilizing information contained in files of the Social Security Administration.
-- jural: households in which all members are applicants for or recipients of supplemental security income | the State agency and the social security office | claim and duty: information, help with a simple application at the social security office, and certification from Social Security Administration files
@ref s 2020(i)(1) (src:1569)
GIVEN `all members of the household are applicants for or recipients of supplemental security income` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(i)(1) the household must be informed of the availability of benefits, assisted in making a simple application at the social security office, and certified from Social Security Administration files` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `all members of the household are applicants for or recipients of supplemental security income` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "households in which all members are applicants for or recipients of supplemental security income"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1571 | Except in a case of disqualification as a penalty for failure to comply with a public assistance program rule or regulation, no household shall have its application to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program denied nor its benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program terminated solely on the basis that its application to participate has been denied or its benefits have been terminated under any of the programs carried out under the statutes specified in the second sentence of section 2014(a) of this title and without a separate determination by the State agency that the household fails to satisfy the eligibility requirements for participation in the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
-- jural: a household | the State agency | immunity: no denial or termination solely because another program denied or terminated it
@ref s 2020(i)(2) (src:1571)
GIVEN `the denial or termination is solely on the basis that the application was denied or the benefits were terminated under a program carried out under the statutes specified in the second sentence of section 2014(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency has made a separate determination that the household fails to satisfy the eligibility requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is a disqualification as a penalty for failure to comply with a public assistance program rule or regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(i)(2) the State agency may deny the application or terminate the benefits` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Except in a case of disqualification as a penalty for failure to comply with a public assistance program rule or regulation" lifts the bar and grants nothing
        IF `the case is a disqualification as a penalty for failure to comply with a public assistance program rule or regulation` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the denial or termination is solely on the basis that the application was denied or the benefits were terminated under a program carried out under the statutes specified in the second sentence of section 2014(a)` AND (NOT `the State agency has made a separate determination that the household fails to satisfy the eligibility requirements`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no household shall have its application to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program denied nor its benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program terminated solely on the basis that"
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "solely on the basis ... and without a separate determination by the State agency"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 2020(j) Notice of availability of benefits and applications; revision of memorandum of understanding`

-- inert: 1572 | reason 1 | the subsection heading (j) "Notice of availability of benefits and applications; revision of memorandum of understanding"
-- src:1573 | (1) Any individual who is an applicant for or recipient of supplemental security income or social security benefits (under regulations prescribed by the Secretary in conjunction with the Commissioner of Social Security) shall be informed of the availability of benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program and informed of the availability of a simple application to participate in such program at the social security office.
-- jural: an applicant for or recipient of supplemental security income or social security benefits | the Secretary and the Commissioner of Social Security | claim and duty: information on the availability of benefits and of a simple application at the social security office
@ref s 2020(j)(1) (src:1573)
GIVEN `the individual is an applicant for or recipient of supplemental security income or social security benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(j)(1) the individual must be informed of the availability of benefits and of a simple application at the social security office` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the individual is an applicant for or recipient of supplemental security income or social security benefits` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any individual who is an applicant for or recipient of supplemental security income or social security benefits (under regulations prescribed by the Secretary in conjunction with the Commissioner of Social Security)"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 2020(j)(2) matter the memorandum of understanding must ensure` IS ONE OF
    `s 2020(j)(2)(A) applicants for and recipients of social security benefits are adequately notified in social security offices that assistance may be available under this chapter`
    `s 2020(j)(2)(B) applications from households in which all members are applicants for or recipients of supplemental security income are forwarded immediately to the State agency in an efficient and timely manner`
    `s 2020(j)(2)(C) the Commissioner of Social Security receives from the Secretary reimbursement for costs incurred to provide such services`
    `s 2020(j)(2) any other matter`

-- src:1574 | (2) The Secretary and the Commissioner of Social Security shall revise the memorandum of understanding in effect on December 23, 1985, regarding services to be provided in social security offices under this subsection and subsection (i), in a manner to ensure that—
-- src:1575 | (A) applicants for and recipients of social security benefits are adequately notified in social security offices that assistance may be available to them under this chapter;
-- src:1576 | (B) applications for assistance under this chapter from households in which all members are applicants for or recipients of supplemental security income will be forwarded immediately to the State agency in an efficient and timely manner; and
-- src:1577 | (C) the Commissioner of Social Security receives from the Secretary reimbursement for costs incurred to provide such services.
-- jural: applicants and recipients of social security benefits | the Secretary and the Commissioner of Social Security | claim and duty: the memorandum of understanding in effect on December 23, 1985 is revised to ensure three things
@ref s 2020(j)(2) (src:1574-1577)
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `s 2020(j)(2) matter the memorandum of understanding must ensure`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(j)(2) the revised memorandum of understanding must ensure the matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    WHEN `s 2020(j)(2) any other matter` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text names three matters and says nothing of others
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `s 2020(k) Use of post offices`

-- src:1579 | Subject to the approval of the President, post offices in all or part of the State may provide, on request by the State agency, supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits to eligible households.
-- jural: eligible households | post offices | privilege: post offices may provide benefits on the State agency's request, subject to the President's approval
@ref s 2020(k) (src:1579)
GIVEN `the President has approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency has requested it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefits are for eligible households` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(k) post offices in all or part of the State may provide supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the President has approved` AND `the State agency has requested it` AND `the benefits are for eligible households` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to the approval of the President, post offices in all or part of the State may provide, on request by the State agency, supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits to eligible households"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 2020(l) Special financial audit review of high participation States`

-- src:1581 | Whenever the ratio of a State’s average supplemental nutrition assistance program participation in any quarter of a fiscal year to the State’s total population in that quarter (estimated on the basis of the latest available population estimates as provided by the Department of Commerce, Bureau of the Census, Series P–25, Current Population Reports (or its successor series)) exceeds 60 per centum, the Office of the Inspector General of the Department of Agriculture shall immediately schedule a financial audit review of a sample of project areas within that State. …
-- jural: the Secretary | the Office of the Inspector General | claim and duty: a financial audit review of a sample of project areas when participation exceeds 60 per centum of the State's population
@ref s 2020(l) (src:1581)
GIVEN `the State's average participation in the quarter` IS A NUMBER
      `the State's total population in that quarter` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(l) the Office of the Inspector General must immediately schedule a financial audit review of a sample of project areas` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State's total population in that quarter` AT MOST 0 THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the ratio of participation to a population of nothing is not defined
        IF `the State's average participation in the quarter` DIVIDED BY `the State's total population in that quarter` GREATER THAN 0.6 THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Whenever the ratio ... exceeds 60 per centum"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1581 | Any financial audit review subsequent to the first such review, required under the preceding sentence, shall be conducted at the option of the Office of the Inspector General.
@ref s 2020(l) (src:1581)
GIVEN `the review is subsequent to the first such review required under the preceding sentence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(l) the Office of the Inspector General conducts the review at its option` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the review is subsequent to the first such review required under the preceding sentence` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any financial audit review subsequent to the first such review"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 2020(m) Alaskan fee agents; use and services`

-- src:1583 | The Secretary shall provide for the use of fee agents in rural Alaska. As used in this subsection “fee agent” means a paid agent who, although not a State employee, is authorized by the State to make applications available to low-income households, assist in the completion of applications, conduct required interviews, secure required verification, forward completed applications and supporting documentation to the State agency, and provide other services as required by the State agency. Such services shall not include making final decisions on household eligibility or benefit levels.
-- jural: households in rural Alaska | the Secretary | claim and duty: fee agents are provided
@ref s 2020(m) (src:1583)
GIVEN `the area` IS AN Area
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(m) the Secretary must provide for the use of fee agents in the area` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the area`
    WHEN `Alaska, rural 1` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Alaska, rural 2` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in rural Alaska" (rural 1 and rural 2 are the USDA's subdivision of rural Alaska, snap-core)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 2020(m) facts about a person who may be a fee agent` HAS
    `the person is a paid agent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a State employee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is authorized by the State to make applications available to low-income households, assist in the completion of applications, conduct required interviews, secure required verification, forward completed applications and supporting documentation to the State agency, and provide other services as required by the State agency` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1583 | As used in this subsection “fee agent” means a paid agent who, although not a State employee, is authorized by the State to make applications available to low-income households, assist in the completion of applications, conduct required interviews, secure required verification, forward completed applications and supporting documentation to the State agency, and provide other services as required by the State agency. …
-- jural: none | none | none: a definition
@ref s 2020(m) (src:1583)
GIVEN `the person` IS A `s 2020(m) facts about a person who may be a fee agent`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(m) the person is a fee agent` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person`'s `the person is a paid agent` AND (NOT `the person`'s `the person is a State employee`)
            AND `the person`'s `the person is authorized by the State to make applications available to low-income households, assist in the completion of applications, conduct required interviews, secure required verification, forward completed applications and supporting documentation to the State agency, and provide other services as required by the State agency` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“fee agent” means a paid agent who, although not a State employee, is authorized by the State to make applications available"

-- src:1583 | Such services shall not include making final decisions on household eligibility or benefit levels.
-- jural: a household | a fee agent | disability: a fee agent cannot make the final decision on the household's eligibility or benefit level
@ref s 2020(m) (src:1583)
GIVEN `the service is making final decisions on household eligibility or benefit levels` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(m) the services of a fee agent may include the service` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the service is making final decisions on household eligibility or benefit levels`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Such services shall not include making final decisions on household eligibility or benefit levels"
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "and provide other services as required by the State agency" leaves the other services to the State agency
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 2020(n) Verification by State agencies`

-- src:1585 | The Secretary shall require State agencies to conduct verification and implement other measures where necessary, but no less often than annually, to assure that an individual does not receive both benefits and benefits or payments referred to in section 2015(g) of this title or both benefits and assistance provided in lieu of benefits under section 2026(b)(1) of this title.
-- jural: the Secretary | State agencies | power and liability: State agencies are required to verify at least annually that no one receives both benefits and benefits or payments referred to in section 2015(g)
@ref s 2020(n) (src:1585)
GIVEN `the verification is to assure that an individual does not receive both benefits and benefits or payments referred to in section 2015(g), or both benefits and assistance provided in lieu of benefits under section 2026(b)(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(n) the Secretary must require the State agency to conduct the verification` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the verification is to assure that an individual does not receive both benefits and benefits or payments referred to in section 2015(g), or both benefits and assistance provided in lieu of benefits under section 2026(b)(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where necessary, but no less often than annually, to assure that an individual does not receive both benefits and benefits or payments referred to in section 2015(g)"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref s 2020(n) (src:1585)
GIVEN `the day of the last verification` IS A DATE
      `the day of the next verification` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- A period test (one year, by the month arithmetic of the daydate library): TRUE on the anniversary, FALSE on the day after.
`s 2020(n) the verification was conducted no less often than annually` MEANS
    `the day of the next verification` AT MOST (`add months` `the day of the last verification` 12)
